		text = "The Five Fingers rarely fight each other in the open. Each is strong enough that a war costs more than anything it could win, and the Wings would like it to stay that way.\n\nWhen it happens anyway, it starts small: a debt, a slight, a title left off a name. Then shutters come down street by street. Fixer Offices stop taking contracts nearby. The noodle stalls stay open and feed both sides, because everyone has to eat.\n\nThese wars end the way they start, with a few people quietly agreeing on something. Whoever picked the winning side gets paid. Whoever picked the other side is remembered.",
